course: dictionary
lesson: 6227
title: A mixture of meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Air is a mixture of gases, mostly nitrogen and oxygen.» Here mixture means things that have been put together. In science, it means something a little more exact.
explain: «A mixture is things mixed together but not joined, so you can get them apart again if you pick the right trick.» The words not joined are the clue. Sand and water can be separated by filtering or sieving, but a mixed-up bag of sweets can be sorted by hand.
explain: Mixture can also mean a feeling. You might feel a mixture of happy and sad on the last day of school. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A mixture is two or more things put together but not joined, so they can be separated again.
fact: Examples of mixtures are sand and water, salt water, trail mix and air.
fact: Ways to separate a mixture include filtering, sieving, using a magnet and letting water evaporate.
fact: «Mixture» can also mean a blend of feelings, such as «a mixture of happy and sad».
fact: «Never mix bleach with other cleaners», because some mixtures give off poisonous gas.
exercise: «Air is a mixture of gases, mostly nitrogen and oxygen.» What is a mixture? | A single pure substance that cannot be changed | A gas that smells bad | *Things put together, but not joined, so they can be separated | Something that only ever has one colour
exercise: «A mixture is things mixed together but not joined, so you can get them apart again if you pick the right trick.» Sand and water are mixed. Which trick would separate them? | Mix them with more water so they join | Wait until they become one new thing | Stir them faster until they join | *Pour the mixture through a filter or a sieve
exercise: «Different cleaning products must never be mixed, because some mixtures give off poisonous gas.» Find and copy one word that means harmful to breathe. | products | mixed | *poisonous | cleaning
test: «Mum stirred the cake mixture before she poured it into the tin.» What does mixture mean here? | A small cake | A metal tin for baking | *Ingredients stirred together to make a cake | A single ingredient, like flour
test: «She felt a mixture of happy and sad on the last day of term.» What does mixture show? | She felt only happy | She was tired and hungry | She felt nothing at all | *She felt two feelings at the same time
exam: Gran says «never mix bleach with other cleaners». Why must they never be mixed? | Because they taste bad | Because some mixtures give off poisonous gas | Because bleach is too expensive | *Because mixing them makes a mixture that is good for cleaning, so they must never be mixed
